From 38d1d8bc1a7c412d42bc8bb2d60f5ee7925b1332 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PyScotch <pyscotch@noreply.invalid>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 09:31:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 022/240] Bugfix: set default empty strategies for all strategy
 parameters [report PyScotch]

The default parameters of the band bipartitioning methods and of the
distributed nested dissection method left one strategy parameter NULL
(`org` of `b` in `bgraph` and `bdgraph`, `osq` of `n` in `hdgraph`).
The parser only warned that the parameter was not set, and any
strategy that did not set it crashed when the method was run, as well
as `stratSave()`: `gmap ... -Mr{sep=m{asc=b,low=b}}`.

Refs: PS2-G04-strategy-parser-3
---
 src/libscotch/bdgraph_bipart_st.c | 4 ++--
 src/libscotch/bgraph_bipart_st.c  | 4 ++--
 src/libscotch/hdgraph_order_st.c  | 6 +++---
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/libscotch/bdgraph_bipart_st.c b/src/libscotch/bdgraph_bipart_st.c
index 3cbbdf8..cf175bf 100644
--- a/src/libscotch/bdgraph_bipart_st.c
+++ b/src/libscotch/bdgraph_bipart_st.c
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@
